{% doc %}
  Collection page results (TE-6 AC1, AC3, AC6, AC7, AC8, AC11, AC12, AC14;
  docs/ui-spec/collection.md §3, §6–§9). Reads the global `collection`.
  columns_mobile columns below 48rem; from 48rem columns_desktop, at most 3; from
  80rem columns_desktop (default 3: with the filter column a card is 292 at 1280,
  336 at 1920, Figma 1:502).

  Toolbar (outside the results partial, so its controls keep their listeners):
  - collection-filter-open opens the dialog of blocks/collection-filters.liquid
    with popovertarget; hidden when the collection has no filters, and from 64rem.
    Partial collection-filter-count inside it renders snippets/filter-count.liquid
    (shared with blocks/search-results.liquid): badge with the number of filters
    applied (aria-hidden) plus the same number as text. Filters applied = all
    active_values + 1 when price_range has a min or a max.
  - Partial collection-count: "{n} products" (collection.products_count, after
    filtering), always shown; tabindex="-1" so JavaScript can move focus to it
    after a page change.
  - Sort select with form="collection-filter-form", so sort and filters submit
    together. Selected: collection.sort_by, then collection.default_sort_by. No
    sort setting (AC3, ES1-T106 #1). Apply button in noscript. Same markup as
    snippets/sort-select.liquid (search toolbar), kept inline because ES1-T365
    TC-04 reads it from this file.
  - collection-status: live region, empty until JavaScript fills it.
  - Hidden (`hidden`) when the collection has no products at all (AC14).
  Below 64rem the toolbar sticks under the header (var(--sticky-top)).

  Partial collection-products (name must match the BE script, ES1-T110) wraps the
  paginate of 24 (window_size 1): active filter chips, then the grid and the
  shared pagination snippet, or one empty state. `data-results-label` on the
  results element holds the translated count for the live region.
  - Chips (AC12): `<ul aria-label="Active filters">`, one link per active value to
    value.url_to_remove, one for the price range to filter.url_to_remove, and
    "Clear all" to collection.url (keeps a sort the shopper chose). Links, so they
    work without JavaScript.
  - Empty states (snippets/empty-state, testid collection-empty): the collection
    has no products (Shop All Products + Browse collections); filters match
    nothing (chips stay, Clear filters); `?page=` past the last page (AC7, testid
    collection-page-empty, "Go to page 1").

  Hooks for BE (ES1-T110), outside the partial:
  - data-label-updating on the root: "Updating products…".
  - template[data-collection-updating]: spinner + that text, to put in place of the
    count while a request runs (role="status" stays on collection-status).
  - template[data-collection-skeleton]: one grid item with the card skeleton;
    clone it once per card shown, set aria-busy="true" on collection-grid.
  - template[data-collection-error]: the error alert (empty-state kind error,
    testid collection-error, button data-retry "Try Again"); put it above the grid
    and keep the old grid.
  A refresh fetches collection-products, collection-count, collection-filter-count
  and collection-filters together, so every number matches.

  Variant items (multi-source collections, TE-3 AC8): same rule as
  blocks/featured-collection.liquid. An item with a parent `product` is a
  variant, and the card gets the parent product plus `variant: item`.

  Card images: all lazy when the collection has a banner image (the banner is
  the LCP element); otherwise the first columns_desktop cards are eager.

  Cards need no JavaScript: swatches are indicators (TE-3 AC2, ADR 0010).

  Test hooks: collection-products (root), collection-toolbar,
  collection-filter-open, collection-filter-count, collection-count,
  collection-sort, collection-sort-apply, collection-status, collection-results,
  collection-active-filters, collection-chip, collection-chips-clear,
  collection-grid, collection-product, collection-empty, collection-page-empty
  (each with -heading, -button, -link from snippets/empty-state), and the hooks
  of snippets/pagination.liquid.

  No collection (block used outside the collection template): a hint in the theme
  editor, nothing on the storefront.

  Self-contained: callers must leave the body empty.

  @example
  {% block 'container', id: 'collection-main' %}
    <collection-filters class="collection-layout">
      {% block 'collection-filters' %}{% endblock %}
      {% block 'collection-products' %}{% endblock %}
    </collection-filters>
  {% endblock %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- if collection == blank -%}
  {%- if request.design_mode -%}
    <div class="collection-products__hint" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
      {{ 'blocks.collection_products.placeholder' | t }}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- else -%}
  {%- liquid
    # Select settings are strings; forloop.index needs a number to compare
    assign columns_desktop = block.settings.columns_desktop | plus: 0
    assign columns_mobile = block.settings.columns_mobile | plus: 0
    assign columns_tablet = columns_desktop | at_most: 3

    assign image_sizes = '(min-width: 80rem) calc(' | append: settings.max_page_width | append: ' / ' | append: columns_desktop | append: '), (min-width: 48rem) calc(100vw / ' | append: columns_tablet | append: '), calc(100vw / ' | append: columns_mobile | append: ')'
    # The filter column takes 3/12 from 64rem, so the grid has 9/12 of the width
    if collection.filters.size > 0
      assign image_sizes = '(min-width: 80rem) calc(' | append: settings.max_page_width | append: ' * 0.75 / ' | append: columns_desktop | append: '), (min-width: 64rem) calc(75vw / ' | append: columns_tablet | append: '), (min-width: 48rem) calc(100vw / ' | append: columns_tablet | append: '), calc(100vw / ' | append: columns_mobile | append: ')'
    endif

    # Same rule as Clear all in blocks/collection-filters.liquid (snippets/filter-count.liquid)
    capture active_filter_count
      render 'filter-count', filters: collection.filters, count_only: true
    endcapture
    assign active_filter_count = active_filter_count | strip | plus: 0

    # Clear all keeps a sort order the shopper chose; the default sort is dropped
    assign clear_url = collection.url
    if collection.sort_by != blank and collection.sort_by != collection.default_sort_by
      assign sort_param = collection.sort_by | url_encode
      assign clear_url = clear_url | append: '?sort_by=' | append: sort_param
    endif

    assign current_sort = collection.sort_by | default: collection.default_sort_by
    assign updating_label = 'blocks.collection_products.updating' | t
  -%}

  <div
    class="collection-products"
    style="--columns: {{ columns_desktop }}; --columns-tablet: {{ columns_tablet }}; --columns-mobile: {{ columns_mobile }};"
    data-label-updating="{{ updating_label | escape }}"
    data-testid="collection-products"
    {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
  >
    <div
      class="collection-toolbar"
      data-testid="collection-toolbar"
      {% if collection.all_products_count == 0 %}
        hidden
      {% endif %}
    >
      <button
        class="button button--secondary collection-toolbar__filter"
        type="button"
        popovertarget="collection-filter-drawer"
        data-testid="collection-filter-open"
        {% if collection.filters.size == 0 %}
          hidden
        {% endif %}
      >
        {% render 'status-icon', name: 'filter' %}
        <span>{{ 'blocks.collection_products.filter' | t }}</span>
        {% partial 'collection-filter-count' %}
          {% render 'filter-count', filters: collection.filters %}
        {% endpartial %}
      </button>

      {% partial 'collection-count' %}
        <p class="collection-toolbar__results" tabindex="-1" data-testid="collection-count">
          {{- 'blocks.collection_products.results_count_html' | t: count: collection.products_count -}}
        </p>
      {% endpartial %}

      <div class="collection-toolbar__sort">
        <label class="collection-toolbar__sort-label" for="collection-sort">
          {{- 'blocks.collection_products.sort_label' | t -}}
        </label>
        <select
          class="collection-toolbar__select"
          id="collection-sort"
          name="sort_by"
          form="collection-filter-form"
          data-testid="collection-sort"
        >
          {%- for option in collection.sort_options -%}
            <option
              value="{{ option.value | escape }}"
              {% if option.value == current_sort %}
                selected
              {% endif %}
            >
              {{- option.name | escape -}}
            </option>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </select>
        <noscript>
          <button
            class="button button--secondary collection-toolbar__sort-apply"
            type="submit"
            form="collection-filter-form"
            data-testid="collection-sort-apply"
          >
            {{- 'blocks.collection_products.sort_apply' | t -}}
          </button>
        </noscript>
      </div>

      <div class="visually-hidden" role="status" data-testid="collection-status"></div>
    </div>

    {% partial 'collection-products' %}
      {% paginate collection.products by 24, window_size: 1 %}
        {%- assign results_label = 'blocks.collection_products.results_count' | t: count: paginate.items -%}
        <div
          class="collection-products__results"
          data-results-label="{{ results_label | escape }}"
          data-testid="collection-results"
        >
          {%- if active_filter_count > 0 -%}
            {%- assign chips_label = 'blocks.collection_products.active_filters' | t -%}
            <ul
              class="collection-chips"
              role="list"
              aria-label="{{ chips_label | escape }}"
              data-testid="collection-active-filters"
            >
              {%- for filter in collection.filters -%}
                {%- assign group_label = 'blocks.collection_products.chip_group' | t: label: filter.label -%}
                {%- if filter.type == 'price_range' -%}
                  {%- if filter.min_value.value != nil or filter.max_value.value != nil -%}
                    {%- liquid
                      assign price_from = filter.min_value.value | default: 0 | money | strip_html
                      if filter.max_value.value != nil
                        assign price_to = filter.max_value.value | money | strip_html
                      else
                        assign price_to = filter.range_max | money | strip_html
                      endif
                      assign chip_value = 'blocks.collection_products.price_range' | t: min: price_from, max: price_to
                      assign chip_name = 'blocks.collection_products.remove_filter' | t: label: filter.label, value: chip_value
                    -%}
                    <li>
                      <a
                        class="collection-chips__chip"
                        href="{{ filter.url_to_remove }}"
                        aria-label="{{ chip_name | escape }}"
                        data-testid="collection-chip"
                      >
                        <span class="collection-chips__group">{{ group_label | escape }}</span>
                        <span>{{ chip_value | escape }}</span>
                        {% render 'header-icon', name: 'close' %}
                      </a>
                    </li>
                  {%- endif -%}
                {%- else -%}
                  {%- for value in filter.active_values -%}
                    {%- assign chip_name = 'blocks.collection_products.remove_filter' | t: label: filter.label, value: value.label -%}
                    <li>
                      <a
                        class="collection-chips__chip"
                        href="{{ value.url_to_remove }}"
                        aria-label="{{ chip_name | escape }}"
                        data-testid="collection-chip"
                      >
                        <span class="collection-chips__group">{{ group_label | escape }}</span>
                        <span>{{ value.label | escape }}</span>
                        {% render 'header-icon', name: 'close' %}
                      </a>
                    </li>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
              <li>
                <a class="collection-chips__clear" href="{{ clear_url }}" data-testid="collection-chips-clear">
                  {{- 'blocks.collection_products.clear_all' | t -}}
                </a>
              </li>
            </ul>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- liquid
            # No products at all, or none left without any filter applied: the collection itself is empty
            assign collection_empty = false
            if collection.all_products_count == 0
              assign collection_empty = true
            elsif paginate.items == 0 and active_filter_count == 0
              assign collection_empty = true
            endif
          -%}
          {%- if collection_empty -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign empty_heading = 'blocks.collection_products.empty_heading' | t
              assign empty_text = 'blocks.collection_products.empty_hint' | t
              assign empty_button = 'blocks.collection_products.empty_cta' | t
              assign empty_link = 'blocks.collection_products.browse_collections' | t
            -%}
            {% render 'empty-state',
              heading: empty_heading,
              text: empty_text,
              button_label: empty_button,
              button_url: routes.all_products_collection_url,
              link_label: empty_link,
              link_url: routes.collections_url,
              icon: 'box',
              testid: 'collection-empty'
            %}
          {%- elsif paginate.items == 0 -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign empty_heading = 'blocks.collection_products.empty_filtered_heading' | t
              assign empty_text = 'blocks.collection_products.empty_filtered_hint' | t
              assign empty_button = 'blocks.collection_products.empty_clear' | t
            -%}
            {% render 'empty-state',
              heading: empty_heading,
              text: empty_text,
              button_label: empty_button,
              button_url: clear_url,
              icon: 'filter',
              testid: 'collection-empty'
            %}
          {%- elsif collection.products.size == 0 -%}
            {%- liquid
              # ?page= past the last page (AC7): the list is empty but the collection is not
              assign first_page_url = collection.url
              assign first_part = paginate.parts | first
              if first_part.is_link
                assign first_page_url = first_part.url
              endif
              assign empty_heading = 'blocks.collection_products.page_empty_heading' | t
              assign empty_text = 'blocks.collection_products.page_empty_hint' | t
              assign empty_button = 'blocks.collection_products.page_first' | t
            -%}
            {% render 'empty-state',
              heading: empty_heading,
              text: empty_text,
              button_label: empty_button,
              button_url: first_page_url,
              icon: 'box',
              testid: 'collection-page-empty'
            %}
          {%- else -%}
            <ul class="collection-products__grid" role="list" data-testid="collection-grid">
              {%- for item in collection.products -%}
                {%- liquid
                  assign card_product = item
                  assign card_variant = nil
                  if item.product != blank
                    assign card_product = item.product
                    assign card_variant = item
                  endif

                  assign card_loading = 'lazy'
                  if collection.image == blank and forloop.index <= columns_desktop
                    assign card_loading = 'eager'
                  endif
                -%}
                <li class="collection-products__item" data-testid="collection-product">
                  {% render 'product-card',
                    product: card_product,
                    variant: card_variant,
                    sizes: image_sizes,
                    loading: card_loading,
                    heading_level: 'h2'
                  %}
                </li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>

            {% render 'pagination', paginate: paginate %}
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      {% endpaginate %}
    {% endpartial %}

    <template data-collection-updating>
      <span class="collection-toolbar__updating">
        <span class="spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        {{- updating_label -}}
      </span>
    </template>
    <template data-collection-skeleton>
      <li class="collection-products__item" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="skeleton-card">
          <span class="skeleton skeleton--media"></span>
          <span class="skeleton skeleton--line"></span>
          <span class="skeleton skeleton--line skeleton--short"></span>
        </div>
      </li>
    </template>
    <template data-collection-error>
      {%- liquid
        assign error_heading = 'blocks.collection_products.error_heading' | t
        assign error_text = 'blocks.collection_products.error_text' | t
      -%}
      {% render 'empty-state', kind: 'error', heading: error_heading, text: error_text, testid: 'collection-error' %}
    </template>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:general.collection_products",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "columns_desktop",
      "label": "t:labels.columns_desktop",
      "info": "t:info.collection_columns_desktop",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "2",
          "label": "t:options.columns.two"
        },
        {
          "value": "3",
          "label": "t:options.columns.three"
        },
        {
          "value": "4",
          "label": "t:options.columns.four"
        }
      ],
      "default": "3"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "columns_mobile",
      "label": "t:labels.columns_mobile",
      "info": "t:info.collection_columns_mobile",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "1",
          "label": "t:options.columns.one"
        },
        {
          "value": "2",
          "label": "t:options.columns.two"
        }
      ],
      "default": "2"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
